G3403.b:
⟪μιμνήσκω⟫
(Bl., -ῄ-, § 3, 3), [in LXX chiefly for ⁨זכר⁩;] ⟪to remind⟫: mid. and pass.;
⟪(a)⟫ ⟪reflexive⟫, ⟪to remind oneself of⟫, hence, ⟪to remember⟫: c. gen. rei, ⟦Matthew 26:75|Mt 26:75⟧, ⟦Luke 1:54|Lk 1:54⟧, ⟦Luke 1:72|72⟧ ⟦Luke 24:8|24:8⟧, ⟦Acts 11:16|Ac 11:16⟧, ⟦2 Peter 3:2|II Pe 3:2⟧, ⟦Jude 1:17|Ju 17⟧; c. neg., of sins, = ⟪to forgive⟫, ⟦Hebrews 8:12|He 8:12⟧ ⟦Hebrews 10:17|10:17⟧(LXX); c. gen. pers., ⟦Luke 23:42|Lk 23:42⟧; seq. ὅτι, ⟦Matthew 5:23|Mt 5:23⟧ ⟦Matthew 27:63|27:63⟧, ⟦Luke 16:25|Lk 16:25⟧, ⟦John 2:17|Jo 2:17⟧, ⟦John 2:22|22⟧ ⟦John 12:16|12:16⟧; ὡς, ⟦Luke 24:6|Lk 24:6⟧; pf., μέμνημι, in pres. sense (cl.), c. gen. pers. (rei), ⟦1 Corinthians 11:2|I Co 11:2⟧, ⟦2 Timothy 1:4|II Ti 1:4⟧; pres., μιμνήσκομαι (only in late writers), c. gen. pers., in sense of caring for, ⟦Hebrews 2:6|He 2:6⟧(LXX) ⟦Hebrews 13:3|13:3⟧;
⟪(b)⟫ in passive sense, ⟪to be remembered⟫, aor., ἐμνήσθην: seq. ἐνώπιον, c. gen. pers. (cf. ⟦Ezekiel 18:22|Ez 18:22⟧), ⟦Acts 10:31|Ac 10:31⟧, ⟦Revelation 16:19|Re 16:19⟧ (cf. ἀνα-, ἐπ-ανα-, ὑπο-μιμνήσκω. The tenses of this verb are from the older μνάομαι).†

G3438.b:
** ⟪μονή⟫, -ῆς, ἡ
(< μένω), [in LXX: I Mac 7:38*;]
⟪1.⟫ in cl.,
	⟪(a)⟫ ⟪a staying⟫, ⟪abiding⟫;
	⟪(b)⟫ ⟪continuance⟫ (LXX, I Mac 7:38).
⟪2.⟫ In late Gk.,
	⟪(a)⟫ ⟪a statson⟫ (Paus.);
	⟪(b)⟫ ⟪an abode⟫: ⟦John 14:2|Jo 14:2⟧, ⟦John 14:23|23⟧;
	⟪(c)⟫ ⟪a monastery⟫ (cf. MM, iii, xvi; so in MGr.).†

G3448.b:
⟪μόσχος⟫, -ου, ὁ,
[in LXX chiefly for ⁨פָּר⁩, also for ⁨שׁוֹר⁩, ⁨עֵגֶל⁩. etc.;]
⟪1.⟫ ⟪a young shoot⟫ or ⟪twig⟫.
⟪2.⟫ ὁ, ἡ, μ., ⟪offspring⟫;
	⟪(a)⟫ of men;
	⟪(b)⟫ of animals; most freq. (as always in LXX), ⟪a calf⟫, ⟪bullock⟫, ⟪heifer⟫: ⟦Luke 15:23|Lk 15:23⟧, ⟦Luke 15:27|27⟧, ⟦Luke 15:30|30⟧, ⟦Hebrews 9:12|He 9:12⟧, ⟦Hebrews 9:19|19⟧, ⟦Revelation 4:7|Re 4:7⟧.†

G3487.b:
⟪νάρδος⟫, -ου, ἡ
(Heb. ⁨נֵרְדְּ⁩, both from Sanscrit narda, v. Boisacq, s.v.), [in LXX: ⟦Song of Solomon 1:12|Ca 1:12⟧ ⟦Song of Solomon 4:13|4:13⟧, ⟦Song of Solomon 4:14|14⟧ (⁨נֵרְדְּ⁩)*;] ⟪nard⟫;
⟪(a)⟫ an Indian plant, ⟪the Nardostachys nardus jatamansi⟫, used for the preparation of a fragrant ointment;
⟪(b)⟫ ⟪ointment of nard⟫: ⟦Mark 14:3|Mk 14:3⟧, ⟦John 12:3|Jo 12:3⟧.†
